## README.md

- A README is normally the first thing someone sees when visiting my GitHub repository.

- It explains what my project is.

- A good README can contain:

    - Project name
    - Description
    - Features
    - Installation instructions
    - How to use the project
    - Technologies used
    - Examples
    - Screenshots
    - Future plans
    - Author information
    - Licence

- Example:

    # My Project

    A Python application that manages tasks.

    ## Features

    - Create tasks
    - Delete tasks
    - Mark tasks as complete

    ## Installation

    pip install -r requirements.txt

- README files normally use Markdown.

